{title: Home on the Range}
{artist: Brewster Higley, 1873}
{key: G}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, americana, cowboy}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Oh, [G]give me a [G7]home, where the [C]buffalo roam
Where the [G]deer and the antelope [D]play
Where [G]seldom is [G7]heard a dis[C]couraging word
And the [G]skies are not [D]cloudy all [G]day

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Home, [D7]home on the [G]range
Where the deer and the antelope [D]play
Where [G]seldom is [G7]heard a dis[C]couraging word
And the [G]skies are not [D]cloudy all [G]day

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
How [G]often at [G7]night, when the [C]heavens are bright
With the [G]light from the glittering [D]stars
Have I [G]stood there a[G7]mazed, and [C]asked as I gazed
If their [G]glory ex[D]ceeds that of [G]ours

{chorus}
